     "options": ["True", "False"], "answer": "True",
     "explanation": "Difference-of-cubes identity."},
    {"type": "TRUE_FALSE", "outcome_code": "10-NIOS-MATH-SPF-04", "difficulty": "EASY", "cognitive_level": "UNDERSTAND", "marks": 1,
     "question": "(a + b)^3 = a^3 + b^3.",
     "options": ["True", "False"], "answer": "False",
     "explanation": "(a + b)^3 = a^3 + 3a^2 b + 3ab^2 + b^3; the cross terms 3a^2 b and 3ab^2 are not zero in general."},
    {"type": "TRUE_FALSE", "outcome_code": "10-NIOS-MATH-SPF-05", "difficulty": "EASY", "cognitive_level": "UNDERSTAND", "marks": 1,
     "question": "The first step in any factorisation problem is to look for a factor common to every term.",
     "options": ["True", "False"], "answer": "True",
